		<label>Type 53 Sniper (PU)</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x54mmR. 10-round detachable mag. Bolt-Action.
		
The Type 53 Sniper is a Chinese bolt-action rifle produced in the 1950s. Not to be confused with the seemingly unrelated Type 53 copy of the Mosin-Nagant, this rifle is a straight-pull bolt action rifle of its own design, bearing a closer resemblance to a Mauser or Carcano design. The rifles were intended to be used as marksman and sniping weapons alongside the shorter Type 53 carbines, but the design was seemingly not very successful, as little historical information on it can be obtained.</description>
